{"status":"ready","content":"Let's solve this step by step:\r\n\r\n1) First, calculate the mean (average) of the dataset:\r\n   • $\\bar{x} = \\frac{9 + 14 + 5 + 4 - 20 - 13 - 5 + 13}{8}$\r\n   • $\\bar{x} = \\frac{7}{8}$\r\n\r\n2) Next, subtract the mean from each data point and square the differences:\r\n   • $(9 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (65)^2 = 4225$\r\n   • $(14 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (105)^2 = 11025$\r\n   • $(5 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (33)^2 = 1089$\r\n   • $(4 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (25)^2 = 625$\r\n   • $(-20 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (-165)^2 = 27225$\r\n   • $(-13 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (-105)^2 = 11025$\r\n   • $(-5 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (-41)^2 = 1681$\r\n   • $(13 - \\frac{7}{8})^2 = (97)^2 = 9409$\r\n\r\n3) Sum these squared differences:\r\n   • $4225 + 11025 + 1089 + 625 + 27225 + 11025 + 1681 + 9409 = 66304$\r\n\r\n4) Divide by $(n-1) = 7$:\r\n   • $\\frac{66304}{7} = 9472$\r\n\r\nTherefore, $\\boxed{9472}$ is the sample variance.\r\n","path":"responses/claude-3-5-haiku/livebench-052-math.txt","size":874,"mtime":1779363911}